{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MhYaBoYCFpnJf5CD1oXDnC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Identity and credential rules\n2\t\n3\t- Normalize identifiers before lookup and persistence; store one canonical representation.\n4\t- Enforce `(provider, identifier)` and provider-subject uniqueness in the database where applicable.\n5\t- Handle duplicate-key races and return a stable conflict without exposing database details.\n6\t- Hash passwords using the configured adaptive password hasher; never encrypt or log plaintext credentials.\n7\t- Keep password hashes and provider secrets out of API responses, events and logs.\n8\t- Compare secrets through established libraries and avoid custom cryptography.\n9\t- Allow multiple provider identities per account without conflating profile data with authentication identity.\n10\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b51249f-7f66-465b-9a4b-fbf4b9aec88f","uuid":"ad01d6f4-a88f-42ee-8f55-85a7568cfeb3","timestamp":"2026-08-07T15:14:21.414Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/cmc/Documents/Memories/ai/skills/implement-auth-security-change/references/identity-and-credentials.md","content":"# Identity and credential rules\n\n- Normalize identifiers before lookup and persistence; store one canonical representation.\n- Enforce `(provider, identifier)` and provider-subject uniqueness in the database where applicable.\n- Handle duplicate-key races and return a stable conflict without exposing database details.\n- Hash passwords using the configured adaptive password hasher; never encrypt or log plaintext credentials.\n- Keep password hashes and provider secrets out of API responses, events and logs.\n- Compare secrets through established libraries and avoid custom cryptography.\n- Allow multiple provider identities per account without conflating profile data with authentication identity.\n","numLines":10,"startLine":1,"totalLines":10}}}
